# 3. Core Architecture

Use a layered Spring Boot architecture.

Recommended structure:

```text
src/main/java/com/example/leavemanagement/

├── config/
├── controller/
├── dto/
├── entity/
├── enums/
├── exception/
├── repository/
├── security/
├── service/
│   ├── LeaveService
│   ├── ApprovalService
│   ├── LeaveBalanceService
│   ├── LeaveProrationService
│   ├── LeaveDayCalculationService
│   ├── ConflictDetectionService
│   ├── EscalationService
│   ├── NotificationService
│   ├── PolicyService
│   ├── AuditService
│   └── LeaveStateMachineService
└── scheduler/
```

Rules:

* Controllers must remain thin.
* Business logic belongs in services.
* Repositories handle persistence.
* DTOs must be used for API requests/responses.
* Do not expose JPA entities directly.
* Use transactions for state-changing operations.
* Use centralized exception handling.
* Avoid duplicated business logic.
* Follow SOLID principles.

